-- title:
--   Node-local functions as quotients integral over (A∩ K)[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ whose vanishing locus is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $a \in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k` (every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$), with $a^{q^2}=a$, $a \neq 0$, $a \neq 1728$. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$. Assume: $f$ and its image under `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` both lie in the localisation of the subring generated by constants from $A$ together with $j$ and $j_q$ at the kernel prime of $\mathrm{red}$, each with reduction lying in the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k)$ generated over $k$ by $j$ and $j_q$ at level $1$ and nonzero there; the reduction of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the first place of `frobNodePair q a` (the place attached to $a$) and is not a unit there. Let $K \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ with $f \in$ `fieldOver (1 * q) K` and $f \in$ `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) (coeffSubring A K) (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`, i.e. $f\,\cdot$ `modularEval` $s_0 =$ `modularEval` $r$ for some two-variable polynomials $r,s_0$ over $A \cap K$ with $s_0$ having nonzero value at $(a,a^q)$ under reduction. Then there exist $p, s$ in `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K` (elements of `fieldOver (1 * q) K` integral over the subring generated by constants from $A \cap K$ and $j$) and a polynomial $s_0$ over $A \cap K$ with $s =$ `modularEval` $s_0$, with nonzero value at $(a, a^q)$, such that $f \cdot s = p$ as Laurent series.
--
--   This supplies, at a supersingular point of the reduction of $X_0(q)$, a presentation of a node-local function as a quotient $p/s$ with numerator and denominator integral over $(A\cap K)[j]$ and with $s$ of nonzero value at the node. It feeds the subsequent analysis of vanishing orders along the two components at such a node.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_exists_mul_eq_mem_jIntegralClosure_of_not_isUnit_frobNodePair.lean

